<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who writes HoneyTools, why it exists, and how affiliate links work on this site."
>
  <h1>About HoneyTools</h1>

  <p>
    HoneyTools is a small, independent site reviewing the AI productivity and
    SaaS business tools that are actually worth paying for. Everything here
    comes from hands-on, everyday use — not press kits or affiliate spec
    sheets rewritten with different words.
  </p>

  <h2>Why This Site Exists</h2>
  <p>
    There's no shortage of "best tools of 2026" lists online, and most of them
    are written by people who never opened the product. HoneyTools takes the
    opposite approach: every review is written by someone who has used the
    tool in real work, for real tasks, over real time — and says plainly
    where it falls short, not just where it shines.
  </p>

  <h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
  <p>
    Reviews, pricing breakdowns, and comparisons for AI and SaaS tools —
    split into short, focused posts rather than one giant post per tool, so
    it's easy to find the specific answer you're looking for (pricing,
    alternatives, a specific use case) without wading through everything
    else.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you sign up or purchase
    through them, HoneyTools may earn a commission — at no extra cost to
    you. This never affects which tools get covered or how they're rated;
    tools are recommended because they're genuinely useful, and affiliate
    relationships (where they exist) are disclosed on every post that
    includes one.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections, or a tool you think deserves a review?
    Reach out at <a href="mailto:hello@myhoneytip.com">hello@myhoneytip.com</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
